import H0mework.NavierStokes.Completion.OmittedScaleTimeResponse

/-!
# Whole-carrier compiler for the complete source-owned nonlinear support

The complete support event is not merely a collection of coordinate
calibrations.  At the unchanged physical state it compiles the entire
finite-source Navier--Stokes tangent without loss:

```text
complete source pair producer
→ source-owned zero-filled support
→ finite Galerkin generator
        =
  whole-lattice unforced vorticity tangent
→ whole-lattice PDE residual = 0.
```

The equality holds on the ambient Fourier carrier, including frequencies
outside the installed finite set.  The key source fact at zero frequency is
proved here from transversality of the actual generated vorticity and
velocity rows.  Away from zero, any nonzero nonlinear row omitted by the
carrier would itself belong to the generated missing-support set and hence
is already installed.

This is the macro faithful compiler at the time-zero source event.  It does
not claim that one fixed finite support remains closed for positive physical
time, nor that shell grammar microsteps are classical time steps.
-/

namespace SaturationMonoid
namespace NavierStokes
namespace
    ThreeDimensionalVorticityCoefficientGeneratedCompleteOmittedWholeCarrierCompiler

open Set
open ThreeDimensionalPeriodicFilteredNavierStokesGenerator
open ThreeDimensionalPeriodicIntegerCharacterCoarseFilter
